## SECTION 6: CONSTRUCTION METHODOLOGY, WORK PROGRAM & QUALITY CONTROL

Our execution methodology utilizes structural steel concrete formwork systems to achieve superior building strength, reduce waste, and accelerate completion of the Milimani Affordable Housing project.

### 6.1 Step-by-Step Construction Methodology Narrative

```
PHASE 1: Mobilization, Site Establishment & Foundations (Month 1-3)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Erect perimeter fencing, main gate control, safety signage, and project 
   office trailers. Install temporary water and 3-phase power supply.
2. Conduct topographical survey verification, establishing benchmark controls.
3. Initiate structural excavation using CAT 320D Excavators down to the 
   bearing stratum.
4. Pour concrete blinding (Class 15/20), lay foundation reinforcement mats, 
   and cast structural pad and strip footings (Class 25/20 structural concrete).

PHASE 2: Structural Frame and Slab Formwork (Month 4-10)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Erect vertical columns and shear wall reinforcement cages.
2. Position high-density shuttering plywood for horizontal beam-and-slab systems.
3. Pour concrete using centralized batching plant and mobile concrete pumps 
   (Class 25/20 concrete), vibrated with mechanical pokers to prevent honeycombing.
4. Implement continuous wet-curing for 7 days post-pour. Maintain strict 
   cube-testing protocols (testing at 7, 14, and 28 days in accredited labs).

PHASE 3: Walling, Roofing & Finishes (Month 11-15)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Lay machine-cut Kisii stone walling in cement-sand mortar (ratio 1:4), 
   including hoop iron reinforcement on alternate courses.
2. Erect structural light-gauge steel roof trusses, anchor to reinforced 
   concrete ring beams, and lay pre-painted IT5 roof profiles.
3. Complete MEP (Mechanical, Electrical, Plumbing) first-fix conduits and pipe 
   chases prior to wall plastering.
4. Execute floor screeding, lay porcelain floor tiling, install aluminum window 
   frames, and apply weather-resistant external paint and internal emulsion coats.

PHASE 4: Infrastructure & External Works (Month 16-18)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Install localized bio-digester systems and lay underground sewer lines.
2. Lay interlocking concrete paving blocks on access roads and walkways.
3. Install perimeter LED streetlights, landscaping, and connection of water 
   supply to main mains. Final inspections, clean-up, and hand-over.
```

