## SECTION 7: SOCIO-ECONOMIC COMMITMENTS (LOCAL CONTENT & AGPO SUBCONTRACTING)

Our Joint Venture is fully committed to national socio-economic growth, targeting high rates of local hiring in Kisumu and subcontracting opportunities for historically underrepresented groups.

### 7.1 Local Content Employment Commitment
To stimulate the Kisumu County economy and transfer skills to local youth:
*   We guarantee that at least **65% of all manual, semi-skilled, and general labor** utilized on the Milimani site will be residents of Kisumu County (exceeding the 60% requirement).
*   We will coordinate with the Kisumu County Labor Office and the local administration in Milimani to recruit, register, and onboard local workers.
*   The project will implement on-site National Industrial Training Authority (NITA) certified training modules for local apprentices in masonry, concrete work, and plumbing.

### 7.2 AGPO Subcontracting Strategy (30% Minimum)
We commit to reserving at least **32% of the project's specialized subcontracts** for companies certified under the Access to Government Procurement Opportunities (AGPO) program:

